[Music]  this isn't the star wars that we're used  to it's the spin-off star wars film  rogue one where a ragtag team of rebels  band together to infiltrate an imperial  base steal the plans for the death star  and then they all die oh yeah spoiler  alert if you haven't seen rogue one yet  but it came out in 2016 so i think we're  fine rogue one is one of the better star  wars films disney has released since  their acquisition of lucasfilm in 2012  but it seems to be mostly overlooked  whenever people talk about star wars  whether it's because it's a spin-off  because of its troubled production or  because of actual issues with the film  itself people seem to have forgotten  about rogue one to understand exactly  why this is the case let's dive into how  the idea for rogue one first came about  john knoll known for his work on the  star wars prequels and the pirates of  the caribbean franchise as well as for  being co-creator of photoshop was the  one who first pitched the story for  rogue one with a story centered on a  single line from the opening crawl in  the original star wars film during the  battle rebel spies managed to steal  secret plans to the empire's ultimate  weapon the death star his original pitch  was titled destroyer of worlds and it  featured a mostly militaristic  self-contained story knoll pitched a  considerably low budget for the film  even suggesting that they recycle sets  from the force awakens there were  several changes made from knoll's pitch  to the final cut we received including  saw gerrera with his somewhat  haphazardly constructed darth  vader-esque suit who was not in the  original pitch as well as director  krennic who was originally supposed to  be scarred terribly on the face but  instead we got the beautiful face of ben  mendelsohn the only characters from the  original group that stayed the same were  jyn erso and k2so both of whom only went  through minor character changes  gareth edwards was brought on as  director known for his previous work on  the indie film monsters and 2014's  godzilla later in 2016 though tony  gilroy was brought on for a seemingly  large amount of reshoots gilroy even  went so far as to say that the film was  a mess before he came on there are quite  a few things from the film's trailers  that didn't make the cut and it seems  like these reshoots and other potential  production issues may have been the  culprit whether or not these changes  were for the better we may never know i  do think however that these changes late  in the game for rogue one's release  could be a factor in why the film tends  to be forgotten or overlooked since the  directors were likely focusing on the  underlying themes of the film and  whether the film was too dark or too  light they seem to have missed the mark  in three critical areas first of all  we're given a passive protagonist in jyn  erso rather than causing things to  happen moving the plot forward things  happen to her jyn first witnesses her  mother's murder then she's recruited  into saw herrera's forces then she's  imprisoned then she's rescued from  prison then she's basically forced to go  on this adventure to get the death star  plans none of this happened because of  choices she made to move the plot  forward so rather than giving us a  motivational sympathetic main character  we got a somewhat one-dimensional  passive protagonist it's this kind of  passivity that can make characters a bit  more forgettable and is likely a  contributing factor as to why rogue one  tends to be forgotten about the next way  that rogue one's creators miss the mark  lies in the common phrase show don't  tell take the first scene we get to see  felicity jones as the character of jyn  it's never shown to us who she has  become since her mother's death or how  she was imprisoned we're just told a  list of what she's done in the past not  shown possession of unsanctioned weapons  forgery of imperial documents aggravated  assault escape from custody resisting  arrest and we get no reaction from her  whatsoever when these crimes are listed  later we're only told about her history  with saw gerrera and we never get to  actually see how this time impacted her  fundamentally since the film tells us  all the things we should know about  these characters rather than showing us  it leaves much of the film's dialogue  feeling pretty dry and without purpose  yet again making the film a little bit  less memorable lastly and most  importantly rogue one fails to build  character investment by the end of the  film we should be fully invested in  these character stories and in their  futures but it's hard to feel bad for  the characters when they all die in the  end because we aren't fully invested in  them yet it makes the sacrifice these  characters made seem a lot less  significant and more like the single  line from the original opening crawl  which barely even mentions them i think  this lack of character investment stems  from the fact that most of their actions  in the first half of the film have  little to no consequences for instance  when the pilot is subjected to torture  from the weird alien thing his mind is  basically broken later in the film  though he snaps out of it and is able to  continue helping the rebellion there are  many things like this in the first half  of the movie where actions don't really  have consequences this lack of  consequences and audience investment in  the main characters has caused many  people to basically forget about the  entire first half of rogue one in the  second half of the movie however the  main characters seem to have a much  better purpose and actually have to face  the consequences of their actions the  film really does regain momentum during  the second half and shows us how a star  wars spin-off can achieve some really  great results one of my favorite things  about the film is that we finally get to  see a star wars story that's not focused  on the skywalker family we get to see  more ordinary people doing simply  extraordinary things there's no jedi no  love story and no skywalkers also  there's no opening crawl instead we open  with michael g aquino's spectacular  score which he wrote in a  record-breaking time of just four weeks  we also got some absolutely stunning  cinematography from greg frazier where  he's able to highlight the war aspect of  star wars in both dark and gritty shots  as well as in light and beautiful shots  we get to see the grey area in a galaxy  where things always seem to be black or  white especially in the character of  cassian andor who is set to get his own  series on disney plus later this year  lastly i just want to mention a couple  of things that i love about this movie  first things first k2so is hilarious and  i hope we get to see more of him in  andor  i'll be there for you  said i had to  next up darth vader's castle on mustafar  way cooler than i could have ever  imagined  be careful not to choke on your  aspirations  director  next krennic and his death troopers i  love ben mendelsohn's take on krennic's  character and the death troopers looked  absolutely terrifying and it's amazing  lastly the hallway scene  chefs kiss utter perfection darth vader  should always be seen like this he  should be known as the most terrifying  person in the galaxy and this scene  could not have been done better not even  when it's done in lego although rogue  one has some pretty serious flaws that  cause many people to overlook the movie  when they think about star wars i'd say  the good things the film brings to the  table certainly outweigh the bad  ultimately though it's up to you to  decide whether rogue one is worth  remembering and whether the film's pros  outweigh the cons i find that answer  vague and unconvincing  anyways that's gonna be all for today if  you like what you saw check out the  video on your screen for some different  content or drop a comment below on  something else you'd like to see also  don't forget to like and subscribe as it  truly does help me out and thanks for  watching rocket riley  [Music]

